# Binary assets are stored byte for byte. Without this, git's text heuristic
# (no NUL in the first 8 KB) read a PDF as text and core.autocrlf=input
# stripped its carriage returns on commit — the deploy's copy then failed the
# Case Review's sha check (Netlify build of main@e52c250, 2026-10-16) while
# the working tree looked clean. Pin the kinds this site serves.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.mp4   binary
*.mov   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.zip   binary
